## Retrieval

Use describe("resources") for the current catalog, then describe the resource.
Follow declared relationships. Do not assume internal tables or undisclosed fields are queryable.
Before assigning agents, use (related inbox-ref "assignable_agents") and follow its pages to inspect inbox eligibility.
Intersect eligible agents with the user's selected agent pool; do not silently substitute other agents. Use returned database IDs.
Use WootQL for filtering, joins, counts, grouping, and ranking. Include the original scope and downstream fields without substitute filters.
The result has kind=page, items (list), item_count (integer), has_more (boolean), query_ref, offset and next_offset.
item_count counts this page, not all matching or analyzed records.
The selected parent set fitting on one page does not mean its related rows fit on one page. Exhaust each independently.
Fetch the next page with `(query-next page)`; #f means exhausted. Query handles last for this turn.
Prefer (query-map function first-page) over handwritten pagination. It calls function with full rows from each page, fetching subsequent pages.
Its result reports processed items/pages, stored result references, progress, status, and whether the query was exhausted.
Processed counts prove callbacks completed, not that their analysis was adequate. Inspect progress and receipts after failure.
Pages can split groups. Merge by stable identity before group-level conclusions.
An ordered first page across many parent records is not one result per parent. Missing groups or empty derived fields can mean later pages were not read.
For per-conversation latest N, query ordered messages and group/take in Scheme; WootQL does not support per-group limits.
Query rows contain selected fields, not ref objects. Build refs from the entity and database ID before fetch, related, or act.
For sequence conditions, retrieve stable chronological order and retain state across pages. Prefer a chronological fold to handwritten
date or string comparison, and decide only after the full relevant sequence is read.
Do not declare data unavailable from a sample, an empty derived field, or one incomplete retrieval path. A blocker requires completed retrieval
or a concrete capability error.
